  [
    id 103
    label "TIDLH2ZOf54"
    step 0
    date "2021-04-14T14:16:25Z"
    title "How Blockchain Works  and What It Is | School of Block"
    description "You have one block. And then another one. And another. They&amp;#8217;re linked forever in an unbreakable chain. Each one has been embedded with data that cannot be rewritten after the fact. But see how easily I can just remove this one block and break that chain? What can we use it for? Why hasn&amp;#8217;t it been possible before and what exactly do we mean by consensus? Let&amp;#8217;s find out.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Sections in this video&amp;#10;0:00&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203; Intro &amp;#8211; hello, blockchain&amp;#10;1:30&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203; A recap of crypto and an intro to blockchain&amp;#10;5:04&amp;#8203; Decision-making on the blockchain: consensus mechanisms&amp;#10;5:33 The history of blockchain &amp;#10;7:11 Byzantine General's Problem &amp;#10;8:58 Public and private blockchains&amp;#10;10:03&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203; The future of blockchain&amp;#10;11:25 There you have it!&amp;#10;&amp;#10;CHECK OUT SCHOOL OF BLOCK&amp;#10;Ledger Academy: https://bit.ly/3jhLxiF&amp;#10;&amp;#10;FOLLOW LEDGER&amp;#10;YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/ledger&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/ledger&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/Ledger&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#8203;&amp;#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/Ledger/"
