    title "Blockchain for Good - Waqar Zaka, World Bank, Indian Government, Adnan Hassan, Tykn, Fairchain"
    description "One of the interesting themes around blockchain is how the technology may be used for good causes. We invited six prominent people in the blockchain industry to talk about how they use blockchain for the better. Sylvain Mignot (Fairchain) talks about the blockchain revolution in the coffee sector. Waqar Zaka (Pakistani TV Star) talks about how he uses crypto mining to help refugees. Aalekh Sharan (Indian Government) talks about the Indian government and its blockchain projects to serve its citizens better. Toufic El Rjula (TYKN) talks about the future of resilient identity. Adnan Hassan (Mecasa Advisors) talks about implementing blockchain technology across 100 small states and Rachel Halsema (World Bank) talks about the World Bank Group Blockchain Lab. Watch this very interesting talkshow with insightful perspectives for changing the world!"
