    date "2021-12-17T16:48:21Z"
    title "Blockchain Explained  How Blocks, Mining, and Transactions Work"
    description "#cryptology, #cryptography, #cryptanalysis, #blockchain&amp;#10;&amp;#10;In this video, we explain how blockchains, e.g. bitcoin, work. We describe in detail blocks, how these are mined in a blockchain, and how transactions are generated and executed in a crypto coin. Using our demo blockchain implemented in CrypTool 2, we simulate our very own blockchain and play with addresses, transactions, and mining.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;The blockchain simulation which we show in the video is now available in the current nightly build of CrypTool 2. It will also be available in the upcoming &amp;#34;Christmas 2021 stable release&amp;#34; of CrypTool 2.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Here, you can find the json visualizer that I used in the video: http://jsonviewer.stack.hu/&amp;#10;&amp;#10;If you are interested in learning the fundaments of cryptology, let me invite you to have a look at our video series about the basics of cryptology, also for beginners: https://youtu.be/jbumW7Ym03o&amp;#10;&amp;#10;You can download the latest version of CrypTool 2 from here: https://www.cryptool.org/en/ct2/downloads"
